cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use BlaBla or its benchmark artifacts, please cite this repository.
title: "BlaBla: executable project memory for coding agents"
type: software
version: 0.5.0-alpha
date-released: 2026-09-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kiborgik/blabla"
authors:
  - family-names: Yakovyshyn
    given-names: Petro
abstract: >-
  BlaBla moves behavioral and structural project intent out of chat context into
  small compiled contracts that coding agents can query and verify. It provides a
  coverage-guided behavior verifier with minimized counterexamples, a static
  structure verifier with language providers, and a layered GREEN/YELLOW/RED
  completion gate. The repository includes a four-stage fresh-context handoff
  benchmark with its methodology, prompts, scorers and results.
keywords:
  - coding-agents
  - verification
  - property-based-testing
  - executable-specification
  - llm
